        "title": {
          "en": "Microsoft Develops AI Tutoring Simulator; OpenAI Expands Educator Programs",
          "zh": "微软开发AI辅导模拟器; OpenAI拓展教育者项目"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "Microsoft Research developed StudentSim for evaluating and improving AI tutoring tools through student learning simulation, while OpenAI expanded its 'AI for Educators' program to Brazilian Portuguese and promoted its 'Study Mode' for active learning.",
          "zh": "微软研究院开发了StudentSim研究系统，用于通过模拟学生学习来评估和改进AI辅导工具，而OpenAI则将“AI for Educators”项目扩展到巴西葡萄牙语，并推广其“学习模式”以支持主动学习。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "Microsoft Research's StudentSim is a research system designed to evaluate and improve AI tutoring tools before real-world testing.",
            "StudentSim models how individuals engage with tutors, providing feedback to enhance tutor performance across subjects like chess, writing, and mathematics.",
            "OpenAI launched its 'AI for Educators' program in Brazilian Portuguese and highlighted 'Study Mode' for supporting active, step-by-step learning."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "微软研究院的StudentSim是一个研究系统，旨在在实际测试前评估和改进AI辅导工具。",
            "StudentSim模拟个体如何与辅导工具互动，为国际象棋、写作和数学等科目的辅导工具性能提供反馈。",
            "OpenAI在巴西葡萄牙语中推出了“AI for Educators”项目，并强调“学习模式”支持主动、分步学习。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "These developments indicate a continued focus within the AI industry on practical applications in education, aiming to improve AI tutoring effectiveness through simulation and expand AI-supported learning accessibility globally.",
          "zh": "这些进展表明AI行业持续关注教育领域的实际应用，旨在通过模拟提高AI辅导的有效性，并扩大AI支持学习在全球范围内的可及性。"
        },
        "source": "Microsoft Research",
        "link": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/simulating-student-learning-for-better-ai-tutoring/"
      },
